before:
The supplied HTML is separate from the CSS.

```html
<p class="note">A protected base rule</p>
```

```css
@layer base, theme;
@layer base { .note { color: teal !important; } }
@layer theme { .note { color: purple !important; } }
```

after:
Both color rules are important. The earlier `base` layer wins, so the note is teal.
```css
@layer base, theme;
@layer base {
  .note { color: teal !important; }
}
@layer theme {
  .note { color: purple !important; }
}
```
